IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- LAYER 1: ATTEMPTS TO PROCURE ABORTION
-- (sections 58 and 59) AND CONCEALING THE BIRTH OF A CHILD (sections 60 and 61).
--
-- This module encodes the Act ALONE.  Whether an act is "unlawful" depends, in the
-- cases where it matters most, on law outside this Act; the text of this Act does not
-- say what makes such an act lawful.  So "unlawfully" is a fact the person states
-- (as everywhere in the Act) and no other statute is brought in.

§ `Attempts to procure Abortion`

§§ `Section 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion`

-- src:97 | 58 Administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion.
-- src:98 | Every woman, being with child, who, with intent to procure her own miscarriage, shall unlawfully administer to herself any poison or other noxious thing, or shall unlawfully use any instrument or other means whatsoever with the like intent, and whosoever, with intent to procure the miscarriage of any woman, whether she be or be not with child, shall unlawfully administer to her or cause to be taken by her any poison or other noxious thing, or shall unlawfully use any instrument or other means whatsoever with the like intent, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable ... to be kept in penal servitude for life ...
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 58 (src:97-98)
-- Two limbs, both needing "unlawfully":
--  (1) "Every woman, being with child, who, with intent to procure her own
--      miscarriage, shall unlawfully administer to herself any poison or other noxious
--      thing, or shall unlawfully use any instrument or other means whatsoever with the
--      like intent";
--  (2) "whosoever, with intent to procure the miscarriage of any woman, whether she be
--      or be not with child, shall unlawfully administer to her or cause to be taken
--      by her any poison or other noxious thing, or shall unlawfully use any
--      instrument or other means whatsoever with the like intent".
-- Limb (2) says "any woman", not "any other woman".  The encoding keeps the text's
-- words, so limb (2) also reaches a woman acting on herself; limb (1) is then
-- contained in limb (2) for the same acts (see NOTES.md, fork 58a).
DECLARE `Conduct under section 58` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a woman who was with child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to procure her own miscarriage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `administered to herself a poison or other noxious thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used an instrument or other means whatsoever upon herself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended to procure the miscarriage of a woman, whether or not she was with child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `administered to that woman, or caused to be taken by her, a poison or other noxious thing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used an instrument or other means whatsoever upon that woman` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 58 (src:98)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 58`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58: limb one, a woman with child acting on herself` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `the person is a woman who was with child`
    AND c's `intended to procure her own miscarriage`
    AND (   c's `administered to herself a poison or other noxious thing`
         OR c's `used an instrument or other means whatsoever upon herself`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 58 (src:98)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 58`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58: limb two, any person acting upon a woman` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `intended to procure the miscarriage of a woman, whether or not she was with child`
    AND (   c's `administered to that woman, or caused to be taken by her, a poison or other noxious thing`
         OR c's `used an instrument or other means whatsoever upon that woman`)

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 58 (src:98)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 58`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58: administering drugs or using instruments to procure abortion` c MEANS
        `s 58: limb one, a woman with child acting on herself` c
    OR  `s 58: limb two, any person acting upon a woman` c

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 58 (src:98)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 58: what the text calls the offence` MEANS felony

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 58 (src:98)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 58: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for life`

§§ `Section 59: procuring drugs, &c. to cause abortion`

-- src:99 | 59 Procuring drugs, &c. to cause abortion.
-- src:100 | Whosoever shall unlawfully supply or procure any poison or other noxious thing, or any instrument or thing whatsoever, knowing that the same is intended to be unlawfully used or employed with intent to procure the miscarriage of any woman, whether she be or be not with child, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable ... to be kept in penal servitude ...
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 59 (src:99-100)
-- "unlawfully supply or procure ... knowing that the same is intended to be unlawfully
-- used or employed with intent to procure the miscarriage of any woman, whether she be
-- or be not with child".  The person need not intend the miscarriage; they must know of
-- the intended use.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 59` HAS
    `unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supplied or procured a poison or other noxious thing, or an instrument or thing whatsoever` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew that it was intended to be unlawfully used or employed with intent to procure the miscarriage of a woman, whether or not she was with child` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 59 (src:100)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 59`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59: supplying drugs or instruments to procure abortion` c MEANS
        c's `unlawfully`
    AND c's `supplied or procured a poison or other noxious thing, or an instrument or thing whatsoever`
    AND c's `knew that it was intended to be unlawfully used or employed with intent to procure the miscarriage of a woman, whether or not she was with child`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 59 (src:100)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 59: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 59 (src:100)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 59: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§ `Concealing the Birth of a Child`

§§ `Section 60: concealing the birth of a child`

-- src:102 | 60 Concealing the birth of a child.
-- src:103 | If any woman shall be delivered of a child, every person who shall, by any secret disposition of the dead body of the said child, whether such child died before, at, or after its birth, endeavour to conceal the birth thereof, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding two years, . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 60 (src:102-103)
-- "If any woman shall be delivered of a child, every person who shall, by any secret
-- disposition of the dead body of the said child, whether such child died before, at,
-- or after its birth, endeavour to conceal the birth thereof": "every person", not only
-- the woman, and the time of the child's death does not matter.  `the person is the
-- woman who was delivered` is carried only so that a test can show it makes no
-- difference.
DECLARE `Conduct under section 60` HAS
    `a woman was delivered of a child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person made a secret disposition of the dead body of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person endeavoured thereby to conceal the birth of the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the woman who was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 60 (src:103)
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct under section 60`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60: concealing the birth of a child` c MEANS
        c's `a woman was delivered of a child`
    AND c's `the person made a secret disposition of the dead body of the child`
    AND c's `the person endeavoured thereby to conceal the birth of the child`

@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 60 (src:103)
GIVETH A Classification
`s 60: what the text calls the offence` MEANS misdemeanor

-- "liable, at the discretion of the court, to be imprisoned for any term not exceeding
-- two years": 24 months.
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 60 (src:103)
GIVETH A LIST OF Sentence
`s 60: the sentences the text states` MEANS
    LIST `imprisonment` (`for a term not exceeding` 24)

§§ `Section 61: blank in this text`

-- src:104 | 61 . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref Offences against the Person Act 1861 s 61 (src:104)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 61: blank in this text` MEANS
    "Section 61 shows only its number and a row of dots; there is nothing to encode."
